// Domain 3 — Policy and objects flashcards (FortiManager 7.6).
export default [
  { id: 'd3-f001', topic: '3.1', front: 'ADOM database vs device database?', back: 'ADOM database: policy packages, shared objects, templates. Device database: each FortiGate\'s full configuration. Installs copy ADOM data into the device database, then push only the diff to the FortiGate.' },
  { id: 'd3-f002', topic: '3.1', front: 'Where are firewall objects stored on FortiManager?', back: 'At ADOM level, shared by every policy package in the ADOM. Editing one marks every package that uses it Modified.' },
  { id: 'd3-f003', topic: '3.1', front: 'How many policy packages can a device/VDOM have assigned at once?', back: 'One. A single package can, however, have many installation targets.' },
  { id: 'd3-f004', topic: '3.1', front: 'What does the Install On column do?', back: 'Restricts one policy to some of the package\'s installation targets. Default value **Installation Targets** = every target of the package.' },
  { id: 'd3-f005', topic: '3.1', front: 'A policy type or object menu is missing in Policy & Objects. First check?', back: 'Policy & Objects > Tools > **Feature Visibility**. Per ADOM by default; `set gui-feature-visibility-mode per-admin` makes it per administrator.' },
  { id: 'd3-f006', topic: '3.1', front: 'Four findings of the policy consistency check?', back: 'Duplication (identical objects), shadowing (fully covered), overlap (partially covered), orphaning (defined but unused).' },
  { id: 'd3-f007', topic: '3.1', front: 'Automatic policy check during install: what does it check and what can it do?', back: 'ADOM setting Perform Policy Check Before Every Install. Checks only added or modified policies; on conflict either Continue Installation or Stop Installation.' },
  { id: 'd3-f008', topic: '3.1', front: 'Find Unused Objects vs Find Duplicate Objects?', back: 'Unused: objects nobody references. Duplicate: same definition, different names, with **Merge** to combine them. Both in the Tools menu.' },
  { id: 'd3-f009', topic: '3.1', front: 'What does `objects-force-deletion` control?', back: '`config system admin setting`. Enabled by default: Delete Anyway works on used objects. Disabled: referenced objects cannot be deleted.' },
  { id: 'd3-f010', topic: '3.1', front: 'Dynamic mapping: when is the default value used?', back: 'Only when the device has no per-device mapping. Without a per-device mapping or a default, the package install fails.' },
  { id: 'd3-f011', topic: '3.1', front: 'CLI tables for per-device and per-platform object values?', back: '`config dynamic_mapping` (per device, `edit "FGT-Branch2"-"root"`) and `platform_mapping`. Scripts using them must run on a policy package, not the device database.' },
  { id: 'd3-f012', topic: '3.1', front: 'Normalized interface: per-device or per-platform mapping wins?', back: 'Per-device mapping has higher priority than per-platform; the first match is used.' },
  { id: 'd3-f013', topic: '3.1', front: 'Another name for a normalized interface?', back: 'Dynamic interface (CLI, JSON API and older documentation; a few GUI messages still say dynamic interface).' },
  { id: 'd3-f014', topic: '3.1', front: 'Wildcard normalized interface characters?', back: '`.` = exactly one alphanumeric character; `*` = zero or more characters. All matching interfaces are installed.' },
  { id: 'd3-f015', topic: '3.1', front: 'Meta fields vs metadata variables?', back: 'Meta fields: extra attributes on objects/admins (System Settings > Advanced > Meta Fields), not usable in scripts or templates. Metadata variables: per-device values, Policy & Objects > Advanced, `$(name)`.' },
  { id: 'd3-f016', topic: '3.1', front: 'Metadata variable resolution order?', back: 'Per-device value first, then the device group value, otherwise the default value. Install Preview shows the resolved value. Global Database uses per-ADOM mapping instead.' },
  { id: 'd3-f017', topic: '3.1', front: 'Per-policy lock: how to enable, and one restriction?', back: '`config system global` / `set per-policy-lock enable` (workspace mode only, default disable). Policies used in a policy block cannot be locked individually.' },
  { id: 'd3-f018', topic: '3.1', front: 'Workflow mode in one breath?', back: 'Only whole-ADOM locks; approval matrix required; lock ADOM, start session, change, submit (auto-unlocks); one approver per group (max 8 groups); no device adds or installs during a session.' },
  { id: 'd3-f019', topic: '3.1', front: 'Workflow: effect of Discard, Repair, Revert?', back: 'Discard: deletes the session and all later ones. Repair: new session with the rejected changes. Revert: new auto-submitted session undoing later sessions.' },
  { id: 'd3-f020', topic: '3.2', front: 'Three versions to distinguish on FortiManager?', back: 'FortiManager firmware, ADOM version (FortiOS syntax of the ADOM database), FortiOS version of each device.' },
  { id: 'd3-f021', topic: '3.2', front: 'Can you edit an ADOM\'s version?', back: 'No. Type and version are fixed at creation; move forward only with an ADOM upgrade (More > Upgrade).' },
  { id: 'd3-f022', topic: '3.2', front: 'Upgrading several ADOMs at once: rule?', back: 'Only ADOMs on the same version (two 7.4 ADOMs, not a 7.2 and a 7.4). Same rule for ADOM Upgrade Readiness.' },
  { id: 'd3-f023', topic: '3.2', front: 'What does ADOM Upgrade Readiness do?', back: 'Reports configuration that is missing or invalid for the new ADOM version (export CSV/PDF). It does not fix anything.' },
  { id: 'd3-f024', topic: '3.2', front: 'When to upgrade the Global Database ADOM?', back: 'Last: after every ADOM that uses a global policy package has been upgraded to a supported version.' },
  { id: 'd3-f025', topic: '3.2', front: 'How do you move a FortiGate to another ADOM?', back: 'As Super_User, edit the destination ADOM > Select Device. The device leaves its old ADOM; import its configuration (or assign a package) in the new one.' },
  { id: 'd3-f026', topic: '3.2', front: 'What stays behind when a device moves ADOMs?', back: 'Its policy package, the ADOM objects, VPN Manager communities and other ADOM-level constructs.' },
  { id: 'd3-f027', topic: '3.2', front: 'What does an ADOM revision contain?', back: 'Policy packages, objects and VPN console settings of one ADOM. Not device settings.' },
  { id: 'd3-f028', topic: '3.2', front: 'ADOM revision Restore: does it change FortiGates?', back: 'No. It reverts the ADOM database only; install afterwards to push the rollback.' },
  { id: 'd3-f029', topic: '3.2', front: 'ADOM revision auto deletion options?', back: 'Keep last x revisions, or delete revisions older than x days. Locked revisions are exempt and cannot be deleted.' },
  { id: 'd3-f030', topic: '3.3', front: 'Default workspace mode?', back: '`workspace-mode disabled`: concurrent ADOM access, several admins can edit the same ADOM at once.' },
  { id: 'd3-f031', topic: '3.3', front: '`workspace-mode` values?', back: '`disabled`, `normal` (workspace all ADOMs), `workflow` (workflow all ADOMs), `per-adom` (each ADOM chooses). Changing it logs you out.' },
  { id: 'd3-f032', topic: '3.3', front: 'Workspace mode: what is read-only until you lock?', back: 'Device Manager and Policy & Objects. AP, VPN, FortiSwitch and Extender Manager need the ADOM lock.' },
  { id: 'd3-f033', topic: '3.3', front: 'Green vs red padlock?', back: 'Green: you hold the lock. Red: another administrator holds it.' },
  { id: 'd3-f034', topic: '3.3', front: 'ADOM lock override?', back: '`set lock-preempt enable` (global, default disable; only meaningful in workspace mode). Lets an admin unlock someone else\'s ADOM; their unsaved changes are discarded.' },
  { id: 'd3-f035', topic: '3.3', front: 'What adds Install and Unlock to the Install Wizard?', back: '`config system global` / `set workspace-unlock-after-install enable` (CLI only, default disable).' },
  { id: 'd3-f036', topic: '3.3', front: 'Release a lock held by an absent admin?', back: 'Dashboard > System Information > Current Session List > Delete, or `diagnose system admin-session list` then `diagnose system admin-session kill <session_id>`. Unsaved changes are lost.' },
  { id: 'd3-f037', topic: '3.3', front: 'What needs the whole ADOM locked (not just a device or package)?', back: 'Adding devices, creating policy packages, creating scripts. Running a script on a device needs only that device locked.' },
  { id: 'd3-f038', topic: '3.4', front: 'Policy package status Modified vs Out of Sync?', back: 'Modified: changed on FortiManager, not installed. Out of Sync: changed on the managed FortiGate.' },
  { id: 'd3-f039', topic: '3.4', front: 'Policy package status Never Installed?', back: 'Assigned package that is not the result of importing this device and has not been installed since assignment.' },
  { id: 'd3-f040', topic: '3.4', front: 'Policy package status Unknown?', back: 'The device configuration was retrieved after the package was imported or installed (for example a retrieve after a FortiOS upgrade).' },
  { id: 'd3-f041', topic: '3.4', front: 'Config status Conflict: two fixes?', back: 'Keep FortiGate: Retrieve Config, then re-import the policy. Keep FortiManager: Install Device Settings (only).' },
  { id: 'd3-f042', topic: '3.4', front: 'Does an import change the FortiGate?', back: 'No. It copies policies and objects from the device database into the ADOM database and creates a package.' },
  { id: 'd3-f043', topic: '3.4', front: 'Import wizard object options?', back: 'Import only policy dependent objects, or Import all objects. Policy Selection: Import All or Select Policies to Import.' },
  { id: 'd3-f044', topic: '3.4', front: 'Import interface mapping rule?', back: 'Every enabled interface needs a Per-Device or Per-Platform mapping to a normalized interface. Option: Add mapping for all unused device interfaces.' },
  { id: 'd3-f045', topic: '3.4', front: 'Use FortiGate value vs Use FortiManager value?', back: 'FortiGate value: updates the shared ADOM object; other devices get it at next install. FortiManager value: keeps the ADOM object; next install overwrites this FortiGate.' },
  { id: 'd3-f046', topic: '3.4', front: 'Install Wizard validation checks?', back: 'Policy and object, interface, installation preparation (plus the automatic policy check if enabled). Devices that fail are skipped.' },
  { id: 'd3-f047', topic: '3.4', front: 'Re-install Policy vs Install Wizard?', back: 'Re-install: package already assigned; offers Install Preview and Policy Package Diff. Wizard: first install, package choice, Create ADOM Revision, Schedule Install.' },
  { id: 'd3-f048', topic: '3.4', front: 'Quick Install (Device DB)?', back: 'Pushes the device database with no preview and no cancel. For zero-touch provisioning or well-understood changes.' },
];
